WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.909
Read the operation
A new operation on the real numbers adds the two numbers, then subtracts two.
To understand it, determine its identity element and its inverses.

2
00:00:13.909 --> 00:00:26.455
Check closure
The result is a real number for any two real inputs. This simple but necessary
check establishes closure of the set.

3
00:00:26.455 --> 00:00:39.000
Find the identity
The identity must leave x unchanged. Write the equation and cancel x on both
sides. The identity is two, not zero.

4
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:52.909
Find the inverse
To find the inverse of x, require the result to equal the identity, two.
Solving gives four minus x, which is a real number.

5
00:00:52.909 --> 00:01:07.273
Check associativity
Associativity remains to be checked. Evaluate both parenthesizations to obtain
the same expression, x plus y plus z minus four, for every three real numbers.

6
00:01:07.273 --> 00:01:21.182
Conclude
The operation is also commutative, since exchanging x and y changes nothing.
Thus we have an abelian group, with every condition checked by calculation.
